# Scorecard kiosk - cloud-init instance identity.
#
# Copy to the FAT boot partition as: meta-data  (no file extension)
#
# The instance-id is the lever that decides whether cloud-init re-provisions.
# If it matches what the unit ran last boot, cloud-init "restores from cache"
# and skips re-applying network config and write_files - even if those files
# changed. Bump it to force a full re-provision.
#
# It appears in TWO places and they must agree:
#   1. here
#   2. the `ds=nocloud;i=<instance-id>` fragment in cmdline.txt
#
# Convention: <product>-<unit serial>-<revision>, so a re-provision is a
# revision bump and stays traceable to the physical unit.

instance-id: scorecard-kiosk-0001-r1
